  "ONE patient, ONE acquisition: no interval is valid on any number (case134_sweep.json#cluster)",
  "detection only: case134 has no agreed level names (VERIDAH read C1-C5 on the lumbar CBCT)",
  "truth = A28 vertebral-body boxes; only the pooled detector was trained on body-convention boxes (real C-ArmLSpine frames); the other three were trained on whole-vertebra boxes, so their level is set by the box convention as much as by the angle (RESCORE.md: the conventions cross on every device) -- read the SHAPE against angle, not the level",
  "four boxes per frame on four consecutive bodies (TotalSegmentator L2 dropped as a duplicate of L1; the sacrum dropped, a 1,431-voxel fragment on this clipped CBCT); at oblique and lateral angles the lower two boxes run over the pedicles (ARC_CHECK item 6), which lowers the IoU a body-tight detection can reach",
  "spin exposure 111 kVp / 12 mA against 77-89 kVp / 25-26 mA for the spot frames: a different exposure mode",
  "the angle bins below -100 degrees hold 28-72 boxes (7-18 frames)"
